      "body": "### Version\n\n23.10.0\n\n### Platform\n\n```text\nMicrosoft Windows NT 10.0.19045.0 x64\n```\n\n### Subsystem\n\n_No response_\n\n### What steps will reproduce the bug?\n\nAfter configuration by command:\n`python configure.py --ninja --openssl-no-asm`\n\n### How often does it reproduce? Is there a required condition?\n\nWindows 10\npython 3.10.11 / python 3.11.9\nMicrosoft Visual Studio 2022 17.4\nnode 22.14.0 / node 23.10.0\n\n### What is the expected behavior? Why is that the expected behavior?\n\nCorrect build.ninja generation.\n\n### What do you see instead?\n\nIn the generated build.ninja files, the flags for generating PCH have the form:\n`build obj\\tools\\msvs\\pch\\node.node_pch.obj: cxx $\n    ..\\..\\tools\\msvs\\pch\\node_pch.cc || obj\\node.actions_rules_copies.stamp\n  cflags_cc = <map object at 0x0000026EC5A79840>`\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_",
